  "source_usage_notes": "Official Java/Oracle documentation is used for language, standard-library, release, security, and JDK-tool claims. Maven, Gradle, and JUnit use their maintainers’ official documentation. Explanations and examples in lesson files are original authored expansions of the supplied outline.",
  "pdf_coverage_notes": [
    "The PDF has 69 pages and was extracted and rendered through all pages. The lesson syllabus is Section B, lessons 1–336 across 32 modules.",
    "All 336 lesson titles and their listed subtopics are carried into the course files. Section C contributes 48 named exercises; Section D contributes nine progressive projects plus the capstone; Section E contributes separate optional specialization tracks.",
    "The overview page states an estimated core workload of 150–250 hours and uses Java 25 LTS as the main baseline. The course keeps that workload range, subject to review."
  ],
  "technical_review_notes": [
    "Current Oracle release notes verify that JDK 27 reached GA on 15 September 2026 and identify primitive types in patterns, instanceof, and switch as the fifth preview (JEP 532). Therefore lesson 335 is explicitly a JDK 27 preview lab, not stable Java 25 core syntax.",
    "The current Oracle Java SE support roadmap identifies Java 25 as an LTS release with Premier Support through September 2030 in the published roadmap. Support offerings can differ by distribution and terms; learners should check their chosen vendor.",
    "The PDF repeats instanceof pattern matching in the control-flow and modern-language modules. Both entries are retained as staged introductions with separate source syllabus numbers.",
    "Several examples in this package describe builds, files, databases, HTTP, profiling, or deployment. Those integrations require local tools/services; course content does not claim that CodeLeaf currently executes Java or deploys Java applications.",
    "No claim is made that generated content is expert-reviewed or production-published. All status flags remain draft pending code execution, subject-matter review, and platform assessment integration."
  ],
  "status": "published"
